=========================================================================
Apache Lucene
=========================================================================

Portions of this module, in particular under
com.naqqa.elasticsearch.analysis, were ported or adapted from Apache
Lucene (https://lucene.apache.org/), including but not limited to:

  - the light/minimal stemmers and normalizers under
    analysis/stem/light (e.g. GermanLightStemmer, GermanMinimalStemmer,
    GermanNormalizer, FrenchLightStemmer, FrenchMinimalStemmer,
    ItalianLightStemmer, DutchLightStemmer, NorwegianLightStemmer,
    NorwegianMinimalStemmer, PortugueseLightStemmer,
    PortugueseMinimalStemmer, RussianLightStemmer, SpanishLightStemmer,
    SwedishLightStemmer, FinnishLightStemmer, GalicianMinimalStemmer,
    RslpPluralStep, ScandinavianFolder, ScandinavianNormalizer),
  - the Porter stemmer under analysis/stem/english/PorterStemmer.java,
    whose underlying public-domain algorithm (M.F. Porter) is implemented
    following Lucene's Apache-2.0 licensed adaptation,
  - the script-specific normalizers/stemmers under analysis/lang/c
    (Arabic, Bengali, Hindi, Indic, Persian, Sorani, Thai
    normalizers/stemmers/analyzer factories, and the Thai dictionary
    tokenizer),
  - the HTML character stripping code under analysis/charfilter/html
    (HtmlStripCharFilter, HtmlStripScanner, HtmlCharacterEntities),
  - the word delimiter filter under analysis/filter/worddelimiter
    (WordDelimiterFilter, WordDelimiterGraphFilter,
    WordDelimiterIterator, WordDelimiterSettings),
  - the ASCII folding data tables under analysis/folding
    (AsciiFolder, AsciiFoldingData),
  - the hyphenation package under analysis/hyphenation (Hyphen,
    Hyphenation, HyphenationTree), itself originally derived by Lucene
    from the Apache FOP (Formatting Objects Processor) project,
  - the synonym handling code under analysis/synonym (SynonymFilter,
    SynonymGraphFilter, SynonymMap),
  - automaton support utilities under analysis/automaton (e.g. IntList).

